 "rule": "Every check a folded workflow job ran is one group here; its step bodies are the original run blocks byte for byte, pinned by sha256, except the repairs listed. A new check is a new group (or a step in one), never a new workflow file.",
 "path_filters": "Dropped: every group runs on every pull_request and push to main (a superset of the original path-filtered runs). workflow_dispatch/schedule triggers are not carried (no manual dispatch, no cron).",
 "repairs": [
  "ci.yml job 'collect' (needs: all test jobs, if: always()) only downloaded the other jobs' artifacts and listed them in the log; it carries no check. It is not a group: each group's own artifact upload (demo-results) is retained by the dispatcher.",
  "demo-suite-runner-v2.demo-suite 'Generate unified report': the run block's python -c is double-quoted, so bash stripped the double quotes in report.get(\"validation\", {}).get(\"overall\", \"N/A\") and the step raised NameError: name 'validation' is not defined on every run (the workflow failed on main). The three keys are backslash-escaped so Python receives them double-quoted inside the single-quoted f-string, which is valid on Python 3.11 and later; nothing else in the step changes.",
  "demo-suite-runner-v2.demo-suite steps 6-10 redirect into outputs/, which did not exist in the repository, so 'Run scalar computation' failed with 'No such file or directory'. outputs/.gitkeep is added; the step bodies are unchanged.",
  "scripts/llm_adapter.py: the provider client is created on first use instead of in __init__, so ci.llm-adapter-tests (which constructs a local adapter and checks its structure, with no provider SDK installed by its job) no longer fails with 'OpenAI package required for local'; a missing SDK still raises the same RuntimeError at the first provider call. No dependency is added.",
  "ci.yml jobs' 'needs: cache-clear' ordering is not carried: every group runs on a fresh runner, which the cache-clear job's rm on an empty workspace never affected."
 ],
 "folded_from_commit": "d86a5a45b0e23a4ab0b9f9027fddf2a99f076376",
